# SUCCESS METRICS
## Care to Cure Patient Retention & Follow-up Management System

---

## 1. Purpose

Defines the specific, measurable KPIs used to judge whether this system is achieving its intended outcomes. These metrics are calculated directly from FRD Section 19 (KPI Calculation).

---

## 2. Core KPIs

| KPI | Formula | Target (Illustrative) | FRD Reference |
|---|---|---|---|
| Attendance Rate | Completed Appointments ÷ Scheduled Appointments × 100 | ≥ 85% | FR-038 |
| No-show Rate | No-show Appointments ÷ Scheduled Appointments × 100 | ≤ 10% | FR-039 |
| Cancellation Rate | Cancelled Appointments ÷ Scheduled Appointments × 100 | ≤ 15% | FR-040 |
| Procedure Completion Rate | Completed Procedures ÷ Applicable Procedure Population × 100 | ≥ 75% | FR-041 |
| Follow-up Compliance Rate | Completed Follow-ups ÷ Required Follow-ups × 100 | ≥ 80% | FR-042 |
| Patient Retention Rate | Returning Patients (within measurement window) ÷ Eligible Patients × 100 | ≥ 70% (window TBD) | FR-043 |

*Targets above are illustrative placeholders for portfolio purposes — in a real deployment these would be set by Care to Cure stakeholders based on historical baselines.*

---

## 3. Secondary / Diagnostic Metrics

| Metric | Purpose |
|---|---|
| Top 5 cancellation/no-show reasons | Identifies the most common root causes of drop-off |
| Repeat drop-off patient count | Flags patients with recurring disengagement patterns (FR-037) |
| Department-level attendance/no-show/cancellation rates | Highlights departments needing process improvement |
| Doctor-level performance metrics | Supports fair, standardized performance review (FR-044) |
| Patient satisfaction score (average) | Tracks whether experience quality is improving alongside operational KPIs |

---

## 4. Success Criteria for the Portfolio Build

Since this is a portfolio demonstration project using synthetic data, "success" is measured at two levels:

**A. Functional Success** — the system correctly calculates all KPIs above from the underlying schema (validated via `03-analytics/retention_analysis.sql` and `05-database/queries.sql`).

**B. Demonstration Success** — the KPIs and dashboards clearly tell a coherent story: given the synthetic dataset, a reviewer (e.g., a hiring manager) can see *where* patients drop off, *why* (reason codes), and *how* the numbers roll up into department/doctor performance and an overall retention rate.

---

## 5. Reporting Cadence (Illustrative)

| Report | Frequency | Audience |
|---|---|---|
| Management Dashboard | Real-time / on-demand | Hospital Management |
| Department Performance Report | Monthly | Department Heads |
| Doctor Performance Report | Monthly or Quarterly | Department Heads, Doctors |
| Drop-off Analysis | Weekly or Monthly | Hospital Management, Patient Experience Team |

